Recurrent Photonic Quantum Reservoir for Volatility Surface Forecasting

This project implements two quantum reservoir computing (QRC) architectures for forecasting swaption volatility surfaces:

Model-1: Recurrent Photonic QRC (Explicit Fock Simulation, no Merlin)

Model-2: Feedback-Driven Photonic QRC (Merlin-based implementation)

Both models operate on PCA-compressed volatility surfaces and reconstruct full Tenor × Maturity grids.

Data Pipeline

Raw surface dimension: 224 (Tenor × Maturity grid)

PCA compression: r = 5

Task: One-step-ahead forecasting

Reconstruction: Inverse PCA → full volatility surface

