Surface-Space Performance
Metric	Value
Surface MSE	1.30 × 10⁻⁵
Surface RMSE	3.61 × 10⁻³
Interpretation

Order-of-magnitude improvement over explicit Fock model.

Stable residual formulation.

Efficient online processing.

Scalable and hardware-compatible.

Core Difference
Without Merlin	With Merlin
Memory in quantum state	Memory via classical feedback
Unitary recurrence	Feedback-driven recurrence
Heavy Fock simulation	Optimized abstraction
Explicit permanent computation	Compiled photonic circuit
Higher compute cost	Scalable
Conclusion

Pure Fock QRC improves over classical baselines.

Feedback-Driven Merlin QRC dramatically improves surface accuracy.

Classical feedback memory is more stable than pure unitary accumulation for financial time series.
